          "The right side becomes {{tsq}}, so $x+{{p}}=\\pm{{t}}$, giving {{r1}} and {{r2}}."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "$\\{ {{r1}}, {{r2}} \\}$"
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Take half the coefficient of $x$, square it, and add that value to BOTH sides."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Your left side should become a perfect-square trinomial before you take square roots."
